. Problem Statement
Analyze student library borrowing records represented as tuples (Book ID, Days Kept, Allowed Days), calculate late return delays, apply progressive fine slabs (Rs.2/day for first 5 days late, Rs.5/day thereafter), and summarize overdue penalties.
2. Objectives
•	Process tuple structured borrowing logs.
•	Determine overdue delay days.
•	Apply tiered fine policies and summarize total outstanding dues.
3. Assumptions
•	Standard borrowing limit is 14 days.
•	Fine rates: 1-5 days overdue @ Rs.2/day, >5 days @ Rs.5/day.
4. Algorithm
1. Read records tuple list: (Book_ID, Days_Kept, Allowed_Days).
2. Overdue Days = MAX(0, Days_Kept - Allowed_Days).
3. If Overdue <= 0 -> Fine = 0.
4. If 1 <= Overdue <= 5 -> Fine = Overdue * 2.
5. If Overdue > 5 -> Fine = (5 * 2) + ((Overdue - 5) * 5).
6. Sum total library fines across all records.
